+    // Air's BranchMul64 form carries a Scratch operand, because ARM64's smulh
+    // sequence needs a staging register the allocator has to provide. This
+    // target does not: emitMul64Overflow stages in the data and memory temps,
+    // which are reserved here and cost the allocator nothing. The operand is
+    // accepted and ignored rather than used, which wastes one Tmp per
+    // BranchMul64 and is deliberate -- using it would need the sequence
+    // reordered around the possibility that Air handed us the same register as
+    // dest, and that is an optimisation with no measurement behind it on an
+    // opcode CheckMul reaches rarely.
+    Jump branchMul64(ResultCondition cond, RegisterID a, RegisterID b, RegisterID, RegisterID dest)
+    {
+        return branchMul64(cond, a, b, dest);
+    }
